fuzz-lib-b-01: `// expect: reject` turns any pin into a parse error.

build.rs::strip_header keeps the `// expect: reject` line above the
program; Subject::parse (graphix-fuzz/src/lib.rs:357) wraps the body as
`use super::*; let result = <body>`, so the marker lands after `=` on the
same line, where a comment is a parse error. Every pin carrying the marker
is therefore refused by the PARSER, whatever its program does.

  graphix-fuzz check fuzz-lib-b-01.gx   -> AGREE (reject)
  (the same program without the marker -> AGREE (trace))

Consequences at HEAD: all 81 `reject` rows in outcome.manifest guard
nothing; two of them are runnable pins mislabeled as rejects
(tvar-lock-jul2026/01_constraint_eq_self_deadlock.gx runs to a trace;
abort-seam-jul2026/01_depth_trip_settled_taint.gx is contained).
